<DocsLayout title="Publishing and revision workflow" description="Save drafts, publish approved copy, and recover safely from revision conflicts.">
  <h1>Publishing and revision workflow</h1>
  <p class="lead">v2 keeps published and draft revisions per locale. Saving edits changes the draft state; publishing promotes the draft when the caller has the <code>publisher</code> role.</p>

  <h2>Workflow</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>An editor opens a same-origin page with <code>?copypatch=1</code>.</li>
    <li>The editor saves text against the current published and draft revisions.</li>
    <li>A publisher reviews and promotes the draft when it is ready.</li>
    <li>The next published read returns the updated locale snapshot.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Conflict handling</h2>
  <p>Save, publish, and discard commands carry both expected revisions. If another mutation wins first, CopyPatch returns <code>409 REVISION_CONFLICT</code> and the latest editor snapshot. Refresh before applying the changes again.</p>

  <p>CopyPatch does not promise an immutable audit log. Keep any audit history required by your organization in the host application or storage operations.</p>
</DocsLayout>
